[10] src/index.js — response body fix (behavior note, not just dead code)
Reason: `return new Response(body)` where `body` was the already-consumed
        Request produced the literal body "[object Request]" (verified with
        node). Telegram only inspects the HTTP status, so the handler now
        returns the conventional "ok". If you need the old behavior, it is:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

      return new Response(body);


